From: O-RAN testbed maintenance
Subject: [PATCH] NR UE: restart the NH chain (NCC 0) on each new AS security context

TS 33.501 6.9.2.1.1: the initial AS security context starts at NCC 0.  The UE
kept rrc->nhcc/nh across an RRCSetup + re-registration, so after one N2
handover (NCC 2) the next context's first N2 handover received NCC 2, matched
the stale nhcc, derived KgNB* horizontally, while the target gNB derived it
vertically from the AMF's NH.  Every SRB1 PDU (RRCReconfigurationComplete)
then failed integrity at the target ("discard NR PDU, integrity failed"), the
target never completed the handover, ue->ho_context stayed, and the next
handover was refused ("Ongoing handover for UE 4, cannot trigger new").

Reset nhcc and nh when the AS Security Mode Command is accepted.

diff --git a/openair2/RRC/NR_UE/rrc_UE.c b/openair2/RRC/NR_UE/rrc_UE.c
index bbfd01e48d..312897a719 100644
--- a/openair2/RRC/NR_UE/rrc_UE.c
+++ b/openair2/RRC/NR_UE/rrc_UE.c
@@ -2529,6 +2529,13 @@ static void nr_rrc_ue_process_securityModeCommand(NR_UE_RRC_INST_t *ue_rrc,
   LOG_T(NR_RRC, "\n");
 
   ue_rrc->as_security_activated = true;
+  /* TS 33.501 6.9.2.1.1: a new AS security context starts a new NH chain at NCC 0.
+   * Without this reset the NCC of a previous context (e.g. 2 after an N2 handover)
+   * survived an RRCSetup + re-registration; the next N2 handover then received
+   * NCC 2 == stale nhcc, derived KgNB* horizontally while the target gNB derived it
+   * vertically from the AMF NH, and every SRB1 PDU failed integrity at the target. */
+  ue_rrc->nhcc = 0;
+  memset(ue_rrc->nh, 0, sizeof(ue_rrc->nh));
   srb_id = 1; // SecurityModeComplete in SRB1
   nr_pdcp_data_req_srb(ue_rrc->ue_id, srb_id, 0, (enc_rval.encoded + 7) / 8, buffer, deliver_pdu_srb_rlc, NULL);
 
